        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Trigwa</i> is a problem solving game with a narrative. Each puzzle tells part of a larger story, which is interwoven and elaborated upon by someone the player will have to make an unwilling truce with...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You, as <i>The Stranger,</i> have heeded the call for help from a faraway land, shunned by most and known for its strange ways and obsession with its once greater past.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solve puzzles in a vast underground tomb spanning several floors and unravel the history of the land, room by room, floor by floor.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>How to play:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game will run using <i>GBCbag 2</i> by EASTPIXEL, a packing app for playing games made to run on a Game Boy. Please note that<i> GBCbag 2</i> is not compatible with the Steam Deck.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Requires Windows 10/11. For Linux and macOS users,  find the file <i>game.gb</i> in the folder <i>&quot;Game&quot;</i> and run it separately in an emulator (Sameboy, bgb or Mesen recommended).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>GBCbag 2 Settings</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Controls:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can set up your preferred controls in Settings -&gt; Controls and Video -&gt; Input, but there are 4 pre-configured control schemes:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >WASD + the Comma key (,) + the Period key (.) + Space bar and Left Ctrl</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Arrow keys + C + X + Space bar + Left Ctrl</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >PS4 controller using the Dpad + X + Square + R1 + L1</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Xbox controller using the Dpad + A + B + Start + Back</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Screen:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fullscreen can be toggled by pressing <i>F11</i>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A few video filters are available in Settings -&gt; Video Filter, and a larger choice of various filters can be set in Settings -&gt; Controls and Video -&gt; Video, and then by checking Override video filter.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Recommended settings are: <i>Fullscreen</i>, <i>LCD Grid</i> and <i>Use bilinear interpolation</i>, and under Controls and Video -&gt; Video; <i>Enable GBC LCD color emulation</i> and <i>Enable LCD frame blending </i>(enabled by default).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't want any filters they can be turned off by entering the above mentioned settings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Trigwa</i> is a problem solving game with a narrative. Each puzzle tells part of a larger story, which is interwoven and elaborated upon by someone the player will have to make an unwilling truce with...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You, as <i>The Stranger,</i> have heeded the call for help from a faraway land, shunned by most and known for its strange ways and obsession with its once greater past.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solve puzzles in a vast underground tomb spanning several floors and unravel the history of the land, room by room, floor by floor.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>How to play:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game will run using <i>GBCbag 2</i> by EASTPIXEL, a packing app for playing games made to run on a Game Boy. Please note that<i> GBCbag 2</i> is not compatible with the Steam Deck.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Requires Windows 10/11. For Linux and macOS users,  find the file <i>game.gb</i> in the folder <i>&quot;Game&quot;</i> and run it separately in an emulator (Sameboy, bgb or Mesen recommended).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>GBCbag 2 Settings</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Controls:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can set up your preferred controls in Settings -&gt; Controls and Video -&gt; Input, but there are 4 pre-configured control schemes:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >WASD + the Comma key (,) + the Period key (.) + Space bar and Left Ctrl</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Arrow keys + C + X + Space bar + Left Ctrl</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >PS4 controller using the Dpad + X + Square + R1 + L1</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Xbox controller using the Dpad + A + B + Start + Back</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Screen:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fullscreen can be toggled by pressing <i>F11</i>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A few video filters are available in Settings -&gt; Video Filter, and a larger choice of various filters can be set in Settings -&gt; Controls and Video -&gt; Video, and then by checking Override video filter.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Recommended settings are: <i>Fullscreen</i>, <i>LCD Grid</i> and <i>Use bilinear interpolation</i>, and under Controls and Video -&gt; Video; <i>Enable GBC LCD color emulation</i> and <i>Enable LCD frame blending </i>(enabled by default).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't want any filters they can be turned off by entering the above mentioned settings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
